WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.425
Lab 2 runs the guide's own validate commands
in a test tenant, never production.

2
00:00:05.425 --> 00:00:08.422
The authors haven't run
them, as the page says,

3
00:00:08.422 --> 00:00:13.000
and the path has no Lab 1 on fixtures,
because the guide has no kit yet.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.695
You need a test tenant licensed for Defender
for Endpoint Plan 2, a reader account

5
00:00:17.695 --> 00:00:22.600
activated through pim, and a ring zero
Windows test device onboarded through Intune.

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.312
Values you supply are in angle brackets.

7
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:30.131
Step one, on your workstation: install
the two Graph modules, connect with the

8
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:34.949
environment for your cloud, and create
a folder for this lab's evidence files.

9
00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:36.837
Step two reads incidents.

10
00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:40.226
As the guide states it, a
pass is up to five incidents,

11
00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:43.937
or an empty list in a new
tenant, with no permission error.

12
00:00:43.937 --> 00:00:48.188
An error naming the role means the
account lacks one of the reader roles.

13
00:00:48.188 --> 00:00:51.773
Step three runs on the test
device, in an elevated session:

14
00:00:51.773 --> 00:00:56.350
query the sense service, and read the
onboarding state from the registry.

15
00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:00.360
Microsoft Learn gives the value
one for an onboarded device.
